==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Super Galaxy Cosmo''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultima Galaxy Cosmo''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Supernova Cosmo''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]], and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other ULTRA SOULS, The Grateful Crane has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
The Grateful Crane's range is too short to efficiently control nasty Floating/Angel melee pushers, and is mostly outclassed by Sanzo, whose Slow works better than Knockback, although he's still a good match against various Cyclones ([[Dark Cyclone|Dark]], [[White Cyclone|White]], [[Divine Cyclone|Divine]] and [[Red Cyclone|Red]]) due to them having even lower range.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Super Galaxy Cosmo's guaranteed [[Knockback]] and incredible range allows him to chip down threats from afar while impeding his targets. This is particularly useful against [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Lizard Cat]], [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Bird Cat]] or [[THE SLOTH]]. However, his attack cycle is too slow for him to meaningfully hinder these threats, and an adequate fighting force is needed to keep them at bay.

Super Galaxy Cosmo actually has marginally higher range than [[Sunfish Jones]] and [[Spacefish Jones]] (850 compared to the Jones' 840) and his status effects target both. However, the tiny range difference makes him a rather inconsistent counter.

When Super Galaxy Cosmo is idle, using your regular [[Cat Cannon]] or Breakerblast will disable enemy hitboxes, which, combined with his speed, can cause him to clip into enemies and lose his range advantage, so you should only use it if you need it for certain purposes that are more important than Cosmo's safety, or during his long attack animation.

==='''True Form'''===
The main reason to get this True Form is to gain a fairly long [[Freeze]] effect. The uptime isn't much, but can create a large window of opportunity for other units to exploit, such as using Awakened Bahamut against [[Winged Pigge]] or swarms of [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s/[[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]].

Cosmo's second improvement is his damage, which increases by 40%. His DPS is still low, but once he gets a hit in, he'll rip a major chunk out of the battlefield. Cosmo is still situational and none of his weaknesses are fixed, though, he can just make up for them better. Overall, the evolution is well worth it, despite the massive catfruit cost. With proper meatshielding, he'll be able to do substantial damage to most of the enemies in the game, and the knockback and freeze against angels/floating can make the difference between possible and impossible stages, especially for newer/intermediate players.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Supernova Cosmo receives many new abilities on top of his already existing ones. First, he now gains an [[Omni Strike]] with a 200 forward piercing range, increasing his effective range to 1,050. This addresses one of his most prevalent issues brought by his long animations, as even a small shift in the frontline may result in him missing. The added forward piercing range gives players with the much-needed leeway for Cosmo to function optimally.

His level 10 [[Wave Attack]] takes this concept and amps it up to eleven. When he hits any enemy within his effective range, he unleashes a wave with extreme coverage. This Wave Attack not only doubles his effective DPS to enemies caught by his initial attack but also guarantees that any non-[[:Category:Enemies with Wave Immunity|Wave Immune enemy]] within 2,133 range takes a guaranteed +100k damage—staggered enemies hit by the initial attack are likely to be hit by the subsequent Wave Attack too—making it far easier to proc his abilities. Target traits are also Knocked Back and Frozen for 5 seconds by the Wave Attack. This wave makes Supernova Cosmo even more proficient at sniping ranged enemies such as [[The Face]] variants, Sunfish Jones variants, [[Calamary]]/[[Cala Maria]], [[Raynard]] and many more. In certain cases, he can even destroy certain Barriers/Shields with his initial attack before the resultant Wave cripples or eliminates the affected enemy.

His [[Sage Slayer]] sees important usage in [[Zero Legends]], specifically as a counter to [[Tarsiriel]], [[Ange Lackey]], [[Prof. Owlbrowley]], and especially [[Sage of Mind Soractes]]. Not only that, he's also just a fantastic generalist anti-Sage with the tremendous stat boosts given to him by the ability. Sage enemies are currently exclusive to specific Zero Legends stages, but this ability will gain further relevance as more Floating/Angel Sages are introduced.

Along with cost reduction and increased health, Supernova Cosmo transforms from a fairly decent unit to an unreasonably powerful one that shatters the difficulty for many stages. While it doesn't unlock any new niches like [[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|CAT-10 Gigapult]], it tremendously improves Supernova Cosmo's performance in his intended role & fixes nearly all of his previous problems. Even though evolving him requires 15 Dark Catseyes and 10 Yellow Behemoth Stones, the value of this Ultra Form far exceeds its cost.

==='''Talents'''===
The main useful talent for Cosmo is '''[[Colossus Slayer]]'''. Due to his naturally high range, he can outrange and stay safe in most Colossal stages. This mainly gives him use against [[Archangel Exiel]], [[Baron Seal]] (who relies on Angel peons for pressure), and [[Great Angel Chibinel]]. Granted, this requires proper defense, as those stages tend to be particularly difficult and push hard. His abilities could work against [[Mega-Mooth|Mega Mooth]], but the second half of his gauntlet features Zombies who could burrow past Cosmo and ignore his range advantage. After unlocking his Ultra Form though, Cosmo's matchups against almost every Colossal become absurdly strong, giving him a purpose on nearly every Colossal Gauntlet save a slightly weaker matchup into [[Omens]] due to their far-reaching Surges.

If this talent is unlocked, then the '''Attack Buff''' Talent is also an option, given that the player has an abundance of NP. Cosmo already has use as a general backliner, and dealing heavy damage to strong peons improves his niche. This especially works out since, even with Colossus Slayer in play, Colossal enemies and their peons can have insane stats. His Ultra Form benefits even more from Attack Buff Talents, since his Level 10 Wave Attack also gains the damage bonus, granting him a soul-shattering 250K damage per hit (including the Wave). '''Defense Buff''', however, is not as high-priority, as Cosmo usually relies on his range to avoid attacks. Furthermore, his Ultra Form already grants him a significant amount of additional health, allowing him more opportunities to reposition which renders this Talent obsolete. For that same reason, '''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' is not strongly recommended, though it could potentially help against unboosted [[Loris]] or the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]], though his damage output in his Ultra Form more than makes up for the abilities he loses when Cursed.

Finally, as well as an immunity to curses, Cosmo himself can gain the ability to '''[[Curse]]'''. This Talent is also iffy, as Curse is not nearly as useful as Knockback or Freeze. In fact, since any targeted enemies will get Frozen anyhow, Curse would barely have any time to shine. It could potentially be useful against enemies such as [[Winged Pigge]], [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]], and Archangel Exiel on the Angel side as well as [[Gobble]] and [[Soractes]] on the Floating side, especially since Curse disables all enemy Toxic attacks. However, as this talent is costly in NP, it might not be worthwhile if other options exist. Notably, Papuu is immune to Freeze and Waves, but not to Curse, so this Talent could potentially help players who struggle on this stage. However, this stage alone should not be a reason to unlock this talent.

==='''Orb'''===
Attack Up against Angels or Floating improves his usage against his target traits with the former being preferable due to the more aggressive nature of Angels. Supernova Cosmo is one of the best users of a Berserker Orb, due to his far-reaching Wave Attack and high damage letting him secure kills on many low to mid-health peons and as a result increasing his nuking potential further.

